  "region_count": 13,
  "regions": [
    {
      "blocks": [
        {
          "block_id": "S1.p1.1",
          "bytes": 1891,
          "literal_span_raw_sha256": "809b20b78db3d6622ed791cdea3adb7bbe1868080f6ab6628969c42783985386",
          "raw_byte_end_exclusive": 49051,
          "raw_byte_start_inclusive": 47160,
          "readview": "We study the problem of sampling from the probability measure \\mu(\\mathrm{d}x)=Z^{-1}e^{-V(x)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x on \\mathbb{R}^{d} , where V\\in C^{2}(\\mathbb{R}^{d}) satisfies, for 0<\\alpha\\leq\\beta ,",
          "tag": "p"
        },
        {
          "block_id": "S1.E1",
          "bytes": 1588,
          "literal_span_raw_sha256": "b5c735fec9494c1dfb15f345b7ccf9c4352e80842308f3e62cc360e36ea2872f",
          "raw_byte_end_exclusive": 50640,
          "raw_byte_start_inclusive": 49052,
          "readview": "\\alpha I\\preceq\\nabla^{2}V(x)\\preceq\\beta I\\,,\\hskip 20.00003ptx\\in\\mathbb{R}^{d}\\,,\\hskip 20.00003pt\\kappa\\coloneqq\\tfrac{\\beta}{\\alpha}\\,. (1.1)",
          "tag": "table"
        },
        {
          "block_id": "S1.p1.2",
          "bytes": 81,
          "literal_span_raw_sha256": "fd5719cfe11a00a5b6f8b4bc20b77ede0ee70f26e81e9b6adf4dc80d6047dc6e",
          "raw_byte_end_exclusive": 50722,
          "raw_byte_start_inclusive": 50641,
          "readview": "The main result of this paper is the following.",
          "tag": "p"
        }
      ],
      "raw_byte_end_exclusive": 50729,
      "raw_byte_start_inclusive": 47126,
      "source_id": "S1.p1",
      "whole_region_raw_sha256": "a9bc657fb926368561ab2657dfbfbf6a7a0ba5b8c2122f8d1fb8510a0a975262"
    },
    {
      "blocks": [
        {
          "block_id": "S2.SS2.p1.1",
          "bytes": 662,
          "literal_span_raw_sha256": "32f65c3fd7b7b1bb4d250acfacbcd6a719e46c43f9d23bc4c821fc67f4c55ef7",
          "raw_byte_end_exclusive": 96221,
          "raw_byte_start_inclusive": 95559,
          "readview": "Our algorithm operates on the augmented distribution underlying the proximal sampler of Lee, Shen, and Tian [ 17 ] . For a scale \\eta\\in(0,1/\\beta] , consider the joint law",
          "tag": "p"
        },
        {
          "block_id": "S2.E6",
          "bytes": 1993,
          "literal_span_raw_sha256": "1f01e27c8eb38fd05a57d820c65ee6b36832171cce845e8cd1b52f4588526375",
          "raw_byte_end_exclusive": 98215,
          "raw_byte_start_inclusive": 96222,
          "readview": "\\pi_{\\eta}(\\mathrm{d}x\\,\\mathrm{d}y)\\propto\\exp\\Bigl\\{-V(x)-\\frac{\\|x-y\\|^{2}}{2\\eta}\\Bigr\\}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\,. (2.6)",
          "tag": "table"
        },
        {
          "block_id": "S2.SS2.p1.2",
          "bytes": 609,
          "literal_span_raw_sha256": "924484e75d2b466b5cec5a63a9a814e76aa622d20f2640418354b4f2eb2a5a76",
          "raw_byte_end_exclusive": 98825,
          "raw_byte_start_inclusive": 98216,
          "readview": "The original proximal sampler algorithm performs Gibbs sampling on \\pi_{\\eta} . Namely, under \\pi_{\\eta} one may generate the joint state as",
          "tag": "p"
        },
        {
          "block_id": "S2.E7",
          "bytes": 1473,
          "literal_span_raw_sha256": "2be554d84baf1f2b796ade05fba49271b5d05e4e8d2d46427d47a6756f85c8f9",
          "raw_byte_end_exclusive": 100299,
          "raw_byte_start_inclusive": 98826,
          "readview": "X\\sim\\mu\\,,\\hskip 20.00003ptZ\\sim\\mathcal{N}(0,I)\\ \\text{independently}\\,,\\hskip 20.00003ptY=X+\\sqrt{\\eta}\\,Z\\,. (2.7)",
          "tag": "table"
        },
        {
          "block_id": "S2.SS2.p1.3",
          "bytes": 2910,
          "literal_span_raw_sha256": "88acd72591b34c91b79748a608c4055defcc626177d46412bb70d6de7b478c32",
          "raw_byte_end_exclusive": 103210,
          "raw_byte_start_inclusive": 100300,
          "readview": "Its X -marginal is \\pi_{\\eta}^{X}=\\mu . Write \\pi_{\\eta}^{Y} for the Y -marginal, so that \\pi_{\\eta}^{Y}(\\mathrm{d}y)\\propto e^{-U_{\\eta}(y)}\\,\\mathrm{d}y ; by ( 2.7 ), \\pi_{\\eta}^{Y}=\\mu*\\mathcal{N}(0,\\eta I) is a Gaussian smoothing of the target. We use superscripts for marginal and conditional laws; in particular,",
          "tag": "p"
        },
        {
          "block_id": "S2.E8",
          "bytes": 2430,
          "literal_span_raw_sha256": "f72b9e301f7145614d1dcdad5cba42f06d2b7a1723a29fa65b1f16555b238584",
          "raw_byte_end_exclusive": 105641,
          "raw_byte_start_inclusive": 103211,
          "readview": "\\pi_{\\eta}^{Y\\mid X=x}=\\mathcal{N}(x,\\eta I)\\,,\\hskip 20.00003pt\\pi_{\\eta}^{X\\mid Y=y}(\\mathrm{d}x)\\propto\\exp\\Bigl\\{-V(x)-\\frac{\\|x-y\\|^{2}}{2\\eta}\\Bigr\\}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\,. (2.8)",
          "tag": "table"
        },
        {
          "block_id": "S2.SS2.p1.4",
          "bytes": 2400,
          "literal_span_raw_sha256": "849c2a1835e03020a514d031b11576bc09edaa8163dd4a453309899e04de0d04",
          "raw_byte_end_exclusive": 108042,
          "raw_byte_start_inclusive": 105642,
          "readview": "Gibbs sampling alternates exact draws from the two conditional laws in ( 2.8 ). The scale \\eta controls the strength of the quadratic coupling potential. Decreasing \\eta makes X and Y more tightly coupled and the conditional law of X given Y more localized and better conditioned, which reduces the cost of conditional sampling. The resulting transitions are also more local, however, and generally require more Gibbs sampling iterations. Thus \\eta balances the cost of each iteration against the number of iterations. The convergence and query complexity are studied further in [ 6 , 9 , 15 ] .",
          "tag": "p"
        }
      ],
      "raw_byte_end_exclusive": 108049,
      "raw_byte_start_inclusive": 95521,
      "source_id": "S2.SS2.p1",
      "whole_region_raw_sha256": "ecd28545b39a6c77249cffa353b5a699aafc5ea5c7e8edc0969dc2be5527840d"
    },
    {
      "blocks": [
        {
          "block_id": "S2.E4.m1",
          "bytes": 876,
          "literal_span_raw_sha256": "7bf5e9042442c52d9d0670edccb7da5f9e65e3adec33251faa00374b14d72a79",
          "raw_byte_end_exclusive": 81973,
          "raw_byte_start_inclusive": 81097,
          "readview": "R_{h}\\coloneqq I-2\\,\\frac{hh^{\\top}}{\\|h\\|^{2}}\\,,\\hskip 20.00003ptR_{0}\\coloneqq I\\,.",
          "tag": "math"
        }
      ],
      "raw_byte_end_exclusive": 81973,
      "raw_byte_start_inclusive": 81097,
      "source_id": "S2.E4.m1",
      "whole_region_raw_sha256": "7bf5e9042442c52d9d0670edccb7da5f9e65e3adec33251faa00374b14d72a79"
    },
    {
      "blocks": [
        {
          "block_id": "S3.E4.m1",
          "bytes": 1391,
          "literal_span_raw_sha256": "30ac2694e6c8c1fe66ffc0cf7f4fc6c4458503b0f75c5a821fb82fd4c023f91a",
          "raw_byte_end_exclusive": 255851,
          "raw_byte_start_inclusive": 254460,
          "readview": "c_{y,\\widetilde{x}}\\coloneqq y-\\eta\\nabla V(\\widetilde{x})\\,,\\hskip 20.00003pth_{\\widetilde{x}}(x)\\coloneqq\\nabla V(x)-\\nabla V(\\widetilde{x})\\,.",
          "tag": "math"
        }
      ],
      "raw_byte_end_exclusive": 255851,
      "raw_byte_start_inclusive": 254460,
      "source_id": "S3.E4.m1",
      "whole_region_raw_sha256": "30ac2694e6c8c1fe66ffc0cf7f4fc6c4458503b0f75c5a821fb82fd4c023f91a"
    },
    {
      "blocks": [
        {
          "block_id": "S3.E6.m1",
          "bytes": 1196,
          "literal_span_raw_sha256": "4774061aec8624cdedcc34e40d06d8647add0a188aa75e727a02343121ffd226",
          "raw_byte_end_exclusive": 267111,
          "raw_byte_start_inclusive": 265915,
          "readview": "x_{t}-c_{y,\\widetilde{x}}=(x_{0}-c_{y,\\widetilde{x}})\\cos t+\\sqrt{\\eta}\\,p_{0}\\sin t\\,.",
          "tag": "math"
        }
      ],
      "raw_byte_end_exclusive": 267111,
      "raw_byte_start_inclusive": 265915,
      "source_id": "S3.E6.m1",
      "whole_region_raw_sha256": "4774061aec8624cdedcc34e40d06d8647add0a188aa75e727a02343121ffd226"
    },
    {
      "blocks": [
        {
          "block_id": "S3.E7.m1",
          "bytes": 864,
          "literal_span_raw_sha256": "b40bba77efd1bb372f4bcc89d338d21475145795111f68693900968f47fb128b",
          "raw_byte_end_exclusive": 269363,
          "raw_byte_start_inclusive": 268499,
          "readview": "(x_{\\pi},p_{\\pi})=(2c_{y,\\widetilde{x}}-x_{0},-p_{0})\\,.",
          "tag": "math"
        }
      ],
      "raw_byte_end_exclusive": 269363,
      "raw_byte_start_inclusive": 268499,
      "source_id": "S3.E7.m1",
