    {
      "blocks": [
        {
          "block_id": "alg1::block0",
          "bytes": 210,
          "literal_span_raw_sha256": "729299e627dc1926be744d5314369e578bcd2025578bf6d9ce01c96b8ef0eb62",
          "raw_byte_end_exclusive": 271750,
          "raw_byte_start_inclusive": 271540,
          "readview": "Algorithm 1 Simulation of the ideal conditional half-turn process",
          "tag": "figcaption"
        },
        {
          "block_id": "alg1.l1",
          "bytes": 575,
          "literal_span_raw_sha256": "ca5a4e4f71cf1c126b6f101b65c8cb61ac5ed7efa8200ce6021b7ed1bdc2fd89",
          "raw_byte_end_exclusive": 272408,
          "raw_byte_start_inclusive": 271833,
          "readview": "1: Input: state (x,y)",
          "tag": "div"
        },
        {
          "block_id": "alg1.l2",
          "bytes": 1168,
          "literal_span_raw_sha256": "72ace13bb980edc9ce97e5fb71d481c0e1c4dd25b82f254ac11db2edd6c30845",
          "raw_byte_end_exclusive": 273577,
          "raw_byte_start_inclusive": 272409,
          "readview": "2: Draw \\widetilde{X}\\sim\\pi_{\\eta}^{X\\mid Y=y} and p_{0}\\sim\\mathcal{N}(0,I) independently.",
          "tag": "div"
        },
        {
          "block_id": "alg1.l3",
          "bytes": 687,
          "literal_span_raw_sha256": "434671c6e9f380150896431635119bd5d452c1e826f8fd1a48a8065ac5cf17e5",
          "raw_byte_end_exclusive": 274265,
          "raw_byte_start_inclusive": 273578,
          "readview": "3: Query \\nabla V(\\widetilde{X}) .",
          "tag": "div"
        },
        {
          "block_id": "alg1.l4",
          "bytes": 520,
          "literal_span_raw_sha256": "d57f9465c0a49108edac12671a52db02dccb1a8a2a1834f4d4372824f49b8b86",
          "raw_byte_end_exclusive": 274786,
          "raw_byte_start_inclusive": 274266,
          "readview": "4: Set x_{0}\\leftarrow x .",
          "tag": "div"
        },
        {
          "block_id": "alg1.l5",
          "bytes": 2304,
          "literal_span_raw_sha256": "93e85415e281571e8182fd730cc33abd345c71d864f270221f127730a62e7851",
          "raw_byte_end_exclusive": 277091,
          "raw_byte_start_inclusive": 274787,
          "readview": "5: Evolve (x_{t},p_{t}) according to \\dot{x}=\\sqrt{\\eta}\\,p\\,,\\hskip 20.00003pt\\dot{p}=-\\frac{x-y}{\\sqrt{\\eta}}-\\sqrt{\\eta}\\,\\nabla V(\\widetilde{X})\\,, (3.8) until t=\\pi .",
          "tag": "div"
        },
        {
          "block_id": "alg1.l6",
          "bytes": 2215,
          "literal_span_raw_sha256": "13089d007c4a34db66a1f2bedb3d352d0f8c30f6990cc42a8a408e24fce85fdd",
          "raw_byte_end_exclusive": 279307,
          "raw_byte_start_inclusive": 277092,
          "readview": "6: During the evolution, generate bounce events at rate \\lambda_{\\widetilde{X}}(x,p)=\\sqrt{\\eta}\\,\\bigl[p^{\\top}[\\nabla V(x)-\\nabla V(\\widetilde{X})]\\bigr]_{+}\\,. (3.9)",
          "tag": "div"
        },
        {
          "block_id": "alg1.l7",
          "bytes": 1193,
          "literal_span_raw_sha256": "ee6e0a9475987f10aa9a0608504a7ee6beb1bd54e0e48525fba4f35a8b2db54c",
          "raw_byte_end_exclusive": 280501,
          "raw_byte_start_inclusive": 279308,
          "readview": "7: At each bounce, set p_{t}\\leftarrow R_{\\nabla V(x_{t})-\\nabla V(\\widetilde{X})}p_{t} .",
          "tag": "div"
        },
        {
          "block_id": "alg1.l8",
          "bytes": 510,
          "literal_span_raw_sha256": "f132980e09ea7fb36542fb32f30357687d7bb6809057d274039794d0cf264224",
          "raw_byte_end_exclusive": 281012,
          "raw_byte_start_inclusive": 280502,
          "readview": "8: return x_{\\pi}",
          "tag": "div"
        }
      ],
      "raw_byte_end_exclusive": 281029,
      "raw_byte_start_inclusive": 271457,
      "source_id": "alg1",
      "whole_region_raw_sha256": "00fa63f86419cb2c484ca2edd8c62aa4fa582ae9957e0b64a2509ac94e3d8463"
    },
    {
      "blocks": [
        {
          "block_id": "S3.Thmtheorem1::block0",
          "bytes": 387,
          "literal_span_raw_sha256": "e3366a9409af8b0721530945f9dcd9adc0659f28a0a2bba8bf9f7ab677d0f198",
          "raw_byte_end_exclusive": 281487,
          "raw_byte_start_inclusive": 281100,
          "readview": "Proposition 3.1 (Well-posedness and stationarity of the conditional phase space process) .",
          "tag": "h6"
        },
        {
          "block_id": "S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1",
          "bytes": 2275,
          "literal_span_raw_sha256": "4508de0d2df228d602b318f1dcb919a5dfeb5c7bcd7b1ac32817f339c50218d7",
          "raw_byte_end_exclusive": 283809,
          "raw_byte_start_inclusive": 281534,
          "readview": "For every fixed y,\\widetilde{x}\\in\\mathbb{R}^{d} and initial phase space point (x_{0},p_{0}) , the event-driven dynamics in Algorithm 1 , with the reference point fixed at \\widetilde{x} , defines a unique non-explosive, time-homogeneous Markov process. The phase space measure \\nu_{\\eta,y} is stationary for this process. In particular, the returned position x_{\\pi} is well-defined almost surely.",
          "tag": "p"
        }
      ],
      "raw_byte_end_exclusive": 283823,
      "raw_byte_start_inclusive": 281030,
      "source_id": "S3.Thmtheorem1",
      "whole_region_raw_sha256": "de6701cbbba6cbbfc73f8e4de8b4048f1f768f64871ec024b82423ec1cf3be6b"
    },
    {
      "blocks": [
        {
          "block_id": "S4.E5.m1",
          "bytes": 2388,
          "literal_span_raw_sha256": "58a97f8391edbb2e11697bd2c71f7a44ed9efe7295b7eba8c3f8da19723b0d9c",
          "raw_byte_end_exclusive": 382301,
          "raw_byte_start_inclusive": 379913,
          "readview": "\\begin{split}x_{t+u}-c_{y,\\widetilde{x}}&=(x_{t}-c_{y,\\widetilde{x}})\\cos u+\\sqrt{\\eta}\\,p_{t}\\sin u\\,,\\\\ p_{t+u}&=-\\eta^{-1/2}(x_{t}-c_{y,\\widetilde{x}})\\sin u+p_{t}\\cos u\\,.\\end{split}",
          "tag": "math"
        }
      ],
      "raw_byte_end_exclusive": 382301,
      "raw_byte_start_inclusive": 379913,
      "source_id": "S4.E5.m1",
      "whole_region_raw_sha256": "58a97f8391edbb2e11697bd2c71f7a44ed9efe7295b7eba8c3f8da19723b0d9c"
    },
    {
      "blocks": [
        {
          "block_id": "A1.SS1.p1.1",
          "bytes": 1132,
          "literal_span_raw_sha256": "c93c391d62d8e5e701fca75be68f6396344bcf8731ef0776d327590ca967542a",
          "raw_byte_end_exclusive": 535158,
          "raw_byte_start_inclusive": 534026,
          "readview": "Fix y,\\widetilde{x}\\in\\mathbb{R}^{d} . In the notation of ( 3.4 ), the bounce rate ( 3.9 ) reads",
          "tag": "p"
        },
        {
          "block_id": "A1.Ex1",
          "bytes": 1385,
          "literal_span_raw_sha256": "333b8b86a8cc7e2e1ebd047ae7a9d26bbc95169f2479003a93f399261b9c5132",
          "raw_byte_end_exclusive": 536544,
          "raw_byte_start_inclusive": 535159,
          "readview": "\\lambda_{\\widetilde{x}}(x,p)=\\sqrt{\\eta}\\,[p^{\\top}h_{\\widetilde{x}}(x)]_{+}\\,.",
          "tag": "table"
        },
        {
          "block_id": "A1.SS1.p1.2",
          "bytes": 765,
          "literal_span_raw_sha256": "90fb789121f18f89462c64b8d712dde73f232c88cc0132c4008a24c64852cdc8",
          "raw_byte_end_exclusive": 537310,
          "raw_byte_start_inclusive": 536545,
          "readview": "The deterministic harmonic flow, namely the solution ( 4.5 ) of ( 3.8 ), and the bounce map are",
          "tag": "p"
        },
        {
          "block_id": "A1.EGx1",
          "bytes": 4225,
          "literal_span_raw_sha256": "f5032feadb1e92f4227ed2251246418f24f9044a60b6fd53a965ed38ef2fe628",
          "raw_byte_end_exclusive": 541536,
          "raw_byte_start_inclusive": 537311,
          "readview": "\\displaystyle\\Phi_{t}^{y,\\widetilde{x}}(x,p) \\displaystyle\\coloneqq\\bigl(c_{y,\\widetilde{x}}+(x-c_{y,\\widetilde{x}})\\cos t+\\sqrt{\\eta}\\,p\\sin t,\\;-\\eta^{-1/2}(x-c_{y,\\widetilde{x}})\\sin t+p\\cos t\\bigr)\\,, \\displaystyle\\mathsf{S}_{\\widetilde{x}}(x,p) \\displaystyle\\coloneqq(x,R_{h_{\\widetilde{x}}(x)}p)\\,,\\hskip 20.00003ptR_{0}\\coloneqq I\\,.",
          "tag": "table"
        },
        {
          "block_id": "A1.SS1.p1.3",
          "bytes": 699,
          "literal_span_raw_sha256": "4906734a0bae9af63cc66bcd7db5561b5cbb0ba434ca489572a7ee2cfa7b4890",
          "raw_byte_end_exclusive": 542236,
          "raw_byte_start_inclusive": 541537,
          "readview": "The bounce map is an involution. Although there is a possible discontinuity at h_{\\widetilde{x}}(x)=0 , this creates no ambiguity because the event rate vanishes there.",
          "tag": "p"
        }
      ],
      "raw_byte_end_exclusive": 542243,
      "raw_byte_start_inclusive": 533988,
      "source_id": "A1.SS1.p1",
      "whole_region_raw_sha256": "717157e13a704f73f9a21f1563bdf86b0a2b4ea0182d280e2da752e8b137f679"
    },
    {
      "blocks": [
        {
          "block_id": "A1.SS1.p2.1",
          "bytes": 1565,
          "literal_span_raw_sha256": "63d237197e5633aaaa4bd8eae657b46c014d51fd127994d636325db67d2411fb",
          "raw_byte_end_exclusive": 543847,
          "raw_byte_start_inclusive": 542282,
          "readview": "Let (E_{n})_{n\\geq 1} be independent \\operatorname{Exp}(1) random variables. Starting from \\zeta_{0}\\coloneqq(x_{0},p_{0}) at time T_{0}\\coloneqq 0 , define recursively",
          "tag": "p"
        },
        {
          "block_id": "A1.EGx2",
          "bytes": 4744,
          "literal_span_raw_sha256": "fe669abcd69e12eee08ffb2c965f8ccc37670ce810b4e2fd528eeadac47edf90",
          "raw_byte_end_exclusive": 548592,
          "raw_byte_start_inclusive": 543848,
          "readview": "\\displaystyle S_{n+1} \\displaystyle\\coloneqq\\inf\\Bigl\\{u\\geq 0:\\int_{0}^{u}\\lambda_{\\widetilde{x}}(\\Phi_{s}^{y,\\widetilde{x}}(\\zeta_{T_{n}}))\\,\\mathrm{d}s\\geq E_{n+1}\\Bigr\\}\\,, (A.1) \\displaystyle T_{n+1} \\displaystyle\\coloneqq T_{n}+S_{n+1}\\,,\\hskip 20.00003pt\\zeta_{T_{n+1}}\\coloneqq\\mathsf{S}_{\\widetilde{x}}\\bigl(\\Phi_{S_{n+1}}^{y,\\widetilde{x}}(\\zeta_{T_{n}})\\bigr)\\,, (A.2)",
          "tag": "table"
        },
        {
          "block_id": "A1.SS1.p2.2",
          "bytes": 1978,
          "literal_span_raw_sha256": "09f9ddea64136444d2c06ba5d635bed3114292fec9c97fd32730bfc4a7ada6fd",
          "raw_byte_end_exclusive": 550571,
          "raw_byte_start_inclusive": 548593,
          "readview": "when S_{n+1}<\\infty . If the set is empty, set T_{n+1}=S_{n+1}=\\infty and stop the recursion. Between jumps, set \\zeta_{T_{n}+t}=\\Phi_{t}^{y,\\widetilde{x}}(\\zeta_{T_{n}}) for 0\\leq t<S_{n+1} .",
          "tag": "p"
        }
      ],
      "raw_byte_end_exclusive": 550578,
      "raw_byte_start_inclusive": 542244,
      "source_id": "A1.SS1.p2",
      "whole_region_raw_sha256": "deaf05e75397a7778841acf49396c564e53e7e90553b45f3bad8e16493d19f73"
    },
    {
      "blocks": [
        {
          "block_id": "A1.SS1.p3.1",
          "bytes": 145,
          "literal_span_raw_sha256": "7d88f2e0ad4c34c0fd528bdd1c975cf71d65823c2bb0fb1efd94193c833bb1e3",
          "raw_byte_end_exclusive": 550762,
          "raw_byte_start_inclusive": 550617,
          "readview": "To prove non-explosion, define the shifted harmonic energy",
          "tag": "p"
        },
        {
          "block_id": "A1.Ex4",
          "bytes": 1713,
          "literal_span_raw_sha256": "b58f8b5406d4d4a404001b1d93ec1a87499c2f62a86e22656549e59a6fda5076",
          "raw_byte_end_exclusive": 552476,
          "raw_byte_start_inclusive": 550763,
          "readview": "H_{y,\\widetilde{x}}(x,p)\\coloneqq\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\bigl\\{\\eta^{-1}\\,\\|x-c_{y,\\widetilde{x}}\\|^{2}+\\|p\\|^{2}\\bigr\\}\\,.",
          "tag": "table"
        },
        {
          "block_id": "A1.SS1.p3.2",
          "bytes": 860,
          "literal_span_raw_sha256": "bfd07a89ff4b7a360dca5e0e57b1940a9d6d8a32cdff46f132186aa69897a078",
          "raw_byte_end_exclusive": 553337,
          "raw_byte_start_inclusive": 552477,
          "readview": "The flow and each bounce preserve this energy. Hence, with \\mathcal{E}\\coloneqq H_{y,\\widetilde{x}}(x_{0},p_{0}) , every state produced by the recursion satisfies",
          "tag": "p"
        },
        {
          "block_id": "A1.Ex5",
          "bytes": 1420,
          "literal_span_raw_sha256": "60bcba6175c149d0676e3a3a335682826dedea369ae33b986453c68066c8e515",
          "raw_byte_end_exclusive": 554758,
          "raw_byte_start_inclusive": 553338,
          "readview": "\\|p\\|\\leq\\sqrt{2\\mathcal{E}}\\,,\\hskip 20.00003pt\\|x-c_{y,\\widetilde{x}}\\|\\leq\\sqrt{2\\eta\\mathcal{E}}\\,.",
          "tag": "table"
        },
        {
          "block_id": "A1.SS1.p3.3",
          "bytes": 1491,
          "literal_span_raw_sha256": "ce47b46c3ede6f7f55dd899683df4c14d1db7e14f06d90b34a6909652577fe88",
          "raw_byte_end_exclusive": 556250,
          "raw_byte_start_inclusive": 554759,
          "readview": "Because \\nabla V is \\beta -Lipschitz, \\lambda_{\\widetilde{x}}(x,p)\\leq\\bar{\\lambda}_{\\mathcal{E}}(y,\\widetilde{x}) throughout the path, where",
          "tag": "p"
        },
        {
          "block_id": "A1.Ex6",
          "bytes": 2083,
          "literal_span_raw_sha256": "d58ee6b4d2a2bdd0a4c961848b0166a5edf316aba1900724151652cccd658e84",
          "raw_byte_end_exclusive": 558334,
          "raw_byte_start_inclusive": 556251,
          "readview": "\\bar{\\lambda}_{\\mathcal{E}}(y,\\widetilde{x})\\coloneqq\\sqrt{\\eta}\\,\\beta\\sqrt{2\\mathcal{E}}\\,\\bigl\\{\\sqrt{2\\eta\\mathcal{E}}+\\|c_{y,\\widetilde{x}}-\\widetilde{x}\\|\\bigr\\}\\,.",
          "tag": "table"
        },
        {
          "block_id": "A1.SS1.p3.4",
          "bytes": 93,
          "literal_span_raw_sha256": "8d6388928d508e646c2bad42e4b5433b38b4b2fe465fea62fab09a7196f33f04",
          "raw_byte_end_exclusive": 558428,
          "raw_byte_start_inclusive": 558335,
          "readview": "Hence,",
          "tag": "p"
        },
        {
          "block_id": "A1.Ex7",
          "bytes": 1908,
          "literal_span_raw_sha256": "dce58599c780d0f17922c16107c58ac3fce2a0659c71b8317ef01e050365820a",
          "raw_byte_end_exclusive": 560337,
          "raw_byte_start_inclusive": 558429,
          "readview": "\\int_{0}^{u}\\lambda_{\\widetilde{x}}(\\Phi_{s}^{y,\\widetilde{x}}(\\zeta_{T_{n}}))\\,\\mathrm{d}s\\leq\\bar{\\lambda}_{\\mathcal{E}}(y,\\widetilde{x})\\,u\\,.",
          "tag": "table"
        },
        {
          "block_id": "A1.SS1.p3.5",
          "bytes": 1209,
          "literal_span_raw_sha256": "fa398ef1e92c95870b9a971a8f1959d3c0514931c36455dd025df770f152a560",
          "raw_byte_end_exclusive": 561547,
          "raw_byte_start_inclusive": 560338,
          "readview": "If \\bar{\\lambda}_{\\mathcal{E}}(y,\\widetilde{x})=0 , the event rate vanishes and there are no jumps. Otherwise, ( A.1 ) implies, for every finite waiting time,",
          "tag": "p"
        },
        {
          "block_id": "A1.Ex8",
          "bytes": 1159,
          "literal_span_raw_sha256": "7b297052ac0e850e5cef0389c9802f89886d43913d8943bced148dd98bf734cd",
          "raw_byte_end_exclusive": 562707,
          "raw_byte_start_inclusive": 561548,
          "readview": "S_{n+1}\\geq\\frac{E_{n+1}}{\\bar{\\lambda}_{\\mathcal{E}}(y,\\widetilde{x})}\\,.",
          "tag": "table"
        },
        {
          "block_id": "A1.SS1.p3.6",
          "bytes": 139,
          "literal_span_raw_sha256": "da37355b8f6774978ec5bb1dc5d01b9495de0113235e05dc63ee7309586529c1",
          "raw_byte_end_exclusive": 562847,
          "raw_byte_start_inclusive": 562708,
          "readview": "If the recursion does not terminate, it follows that",
          "tag": "p"
        },
        {
          "block_id": "A1.Ex9",
          "bytes": 1268,
          "literal_span_raw_sha256": "9aece5e3e4962e03be2aa4d46452bbea0cc40d16578458e8110bf3ef56e5000c",
          "raw_byte_end_exclusive": 564116,
          "raw_byte_start_inclusive": 562848,
          "readview": "T_{n}\\geq\\frac{\\sum_{j=1}^{n}E_{j}}{\\bar{\\lambda}_{\\mathcal{E}}(y,\\widetilde{x})}\\longrightarrow\\infty",
          "tag": "table"
        },
        {
          "block_id": "A1.SS1.p3.7",
          "bytes": 759,
          "literal_span_raw_sha256": "403d8ba6092b60dce9b3bbdc1c10f07530b20434920a058df2bc236adac0d4e3",
          "raw_byte_end_exclusive": 564876,
          "raw_byte_start_inclusive": 564117,
          "readview": "almost surely by the strong law of large numbers. Thus, the jump times cannot accumulate, and the recursive construction defines a unique process for all t\\geq 0 . Finally, the memoryless property of the exponential clocks gives the time-homogeneous Markov property. This is precisely the integrated hazard construction of Davis [ 12 , Section 2] . ∎",
          "tag": "p"
        }
      ],
      "raw_byte_end_exclusive": 564883,
      "raw_byte_start_inclusive": 550579,
      "source_id": "A1.SS1.p3",
      "whole_region_raw_sha256": "831b561c07be5a0b17321aea9f6333e77431dde0b0165a1fd60c8cda9fa883f6"
    },
    {
      "blocks": [
        {
          "block_id": "A1.Thmtheorem2::block0",
          "bytes": 375,
          "literal_span_raw_sha256": "da5d65fc41079e1a0eebb7432f9edc60062859a01c6a67d2003428827e7b0799",
          "raw_byte_end_exclusive": 654060,
          "raw_byte_start_inclusive": 653685,
          "readview": "Proposition A.2 (Joint measurability and augmented space half-turn operator) .",
          "tag": "h6"
        },
        {
          "block_id": "A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.1",
          "bytes": 2211,
          "literal_span_raw_sha256": "a1fbac52f3c5caeef9bfc69002262dc5dfbd1b4282b6e64dcb7bd1d6a8819a9f",
          "raw_byte_end_exclusive": 656318,
          "raw_byte_start_inclusive": 654107,
          "readview": "The family of conditional half-turn kernels (\\mathcal{H}_{y})_{y\\in\\mathbb{R}^{d}} admits a version, again denoted by \\mathcal{H}_{y}(x,\\mathrm{d}x^{\\prime}) , such that (y,x)\\mapsto\\mathcal{H}_{y}(x,A) is Borel measurable for every Borel set A\\subset\\mathbb{R}^{d} . Consequently,",
          "tag": "p"
        },
        {
          "block_id": "A1.E9",
          "bytes": 1732,
          "literal_span_raw_sha256": "6c3a2ce2fde9aa26b9178a94ba7f203e06163f3dbb9be77998ea7b411a722641",
          "raw_byte_end_exclusive": 658051,
          "raw_byte_start_inclusive": 656319,
          "readview": "(\\mathsf{H}f)(x,y)\\coloneqq\\int_{\\mathbb{R}^{d}}f(x^{\\prime},y)\\,\\mathcal{H}_{y}(x,\\mathrm{d}x^{\\prime}) (A.9)",
          "tag": "table"
        },
        {
          "block_id": "A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.2",
          "bytes": 564,
          "literal_span_raw_sha256": "f83e1688b6de88aa32d26b6e29de96b6e47ccebf39679a544b211137f6435b50",
          "raw_byte_end_exclusive": 658616,
          "raw_byte_start_inclusive": 658052,
          "readview": "defines a self-adjoint Markov contraction on L^{2}(\\pi_{\\eta}) .",
          "tag": "p"
        }
      ],
      "raw_byte_end_exclusive": 658630,
      "raw_byte_start_inclusive": 653615,
      "source_id": "A1.Thmtheorem2",
      "whole_region_raw_sha256": "385cdf482825c8629611ed5216e114609387383571b5d42a4d35c8ec645a97f3"
    }
  ],
